WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.857 --> 00:00:03.760
A too-light carton from line 3 goes in the bin.

2
00:00:04.457 --> 00:00:05.490
That costs money.

3
00:00:06.474 --> 00:00:09.632
The module Cost engineering is about what something

4
00:00:09.713 --> 00:00:12.395
really costs and whether a fix is worth it.

5
00:00:13.452 --> 00:00:14.683
You are the engineer.

6
00:00:15.378 --> 00:00:19.058
After the shift you and the team lead work out what it costs.

7
00:00:20.057 --> 00:00:23.703
First you know what a carton costs and which decisions follow.

8
00:00:24.732 --> 00:00:27.611
Then you judge the fix and make the saving credible.

9
00:00:28.906 --> 00:00:31.901
The first topic is Cost price and hour rates.

10
00:00:32.614 --> 00:00:35.389
You build up a carton’s cost price from the bottom.

11
00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:41.600
Every line is a quantity times a rate, such as machine time times an hour rate.

12
00:00:42.661 --> 00:00:47.247
A carton that goes in the bin late carries all the cost already put into it.

13
00:00:48.292 --> 00:00:52.205
You often spread the indirect costs with an overhead surcharge.

14
00:00:53.521 --> 00:00:56.400
The second topic is Relevant costs and pricing.

15
00:00:57.143 --> 00:00:58.652
With it you make decisions.

16
00:00:59.665 --> 00:01:03.485
In a decision only the costs that differ between the options count.

17
00:01:04.539 --> 00:01:07.221
Fixed costs stay the same in the short term.

18
00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.302
Variable costs move with every carton.

19
00:01:11.328 --> 00:01:14.451
You determine the contribution margin of a good carton.

20
00:01:15.763 --> 00:01:18.131
The third topic is Investment appraisal.

21
00:01:18.827 --> 00:01:21.579
You spend on a fix once, for years of use.

22
00:01:22.585 --> 00:01:26.706
A saving only counts if money really stops going out or comes in.

23
00:01:27.684 --> 00:01:30.203
On the laptop you work out the cash saving.

24
00:01:31.216 --> 00:01:35.140
On the sheet you put the investment next to the cash saving per year.

25
00:01:36.444 --> 00:01:39.196
The fourth topic is Lean accounting and savings.

26
00:01:39.935 --> 00:01:41.618
You turn waste into money.

27
00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:44.343
A carton in the bin is waste.

28
00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:47.137
You price it at what is really lost.

29
00:01:48.169 --> 00:01:50.595
You add up the cost of poor quality of the bin.

30
00:01:51.589 --> 00:01:55.502
That is how you know what line 3 costs and whether the fix pays.

31
00:01:56.803 --> 00:01:57.581
The whole map.

32
00:01:58.329 --> 00:02:02.369
The third station is Cost engineering, in Making the plant better.

33
00:02:03.415 --> 00:02:05.156
Each topic has four levels.

34
00:02:06.176 --> 00:02:09.705
Start at Basics level with building up the cost of a part.

35
00:02:10.487 --> 00:02:12.333
It shows where costs come from.

36
00:02:13.385 --> 00:02:16.334
At Working knowledge level come the machine hour rate,

37
00:02:16.462 --> 00:02:19.678
payback time, waste in euros and make or buy.

38
00:02:20.702 --> 00:02:24.521
At Advanced level come costs by activity, the price floor,

39
00:02:24.696 --> 00:02:27.157
net present value and the absorption trap.

40
00:02:28.203 --> 00:02:30.513
At Expert level come reading a quote,

41
00:02:30.699 --> 00:02:34.681
customer profit, the investment board and getting savings signed.
